<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Calabria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Calabria is a region of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> forming the 'toe' of the Italian peninsula, with Catanzaro as its capital. In antiquity its coasts held Greek colonies such as Rhegion, Croton and Locri. It was later held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a>, conquered by the Normans in the 11th century and formed part of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> and then of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/calabria.jpg" alt="Calabria" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TUBS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Calabria_in_Italy.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
